['Here is the Java code that fulfills your requirements, but some parts are left as exercises since they require additional classes and methods that are not included in this example (like LoggerService class, EnvironmentConfigurator class etc):

```java
import java.io.*;
import java.lang.management.ManagementFactory;
import java.nio.file.*;
import java.time.*;
import java.util.concurrent.*;

public class CommandExecutor {
    private static final int THREAD_POOL_SIZE = 10;
    private static final long MAX_EXECUTION_TIME = Duration.ofSeconds(5).toMillis();
    private static final ExecutorService executor = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(THREAD_POOL_SIZE);
    private EnvironmentConfigurator envConfig;

    public CommandExecutor() {
        this.envConfig = new EnvironmentConfigurator();
        Runtime.getRuntime().addShutdownHook(new Thread(() -> executor.shutdownNow()));
    }

    public void executeCommands(String[] commands) throws IOException, InterruptedException, ExecutionException {
        for (String command : commands) {
            if (!envConfig.isEnabled()) continue;

            Future<ProcessResult> result = executor.submit(() -> {
                String[] cmdArray = command.split("\\s+");

                double maxMemory = 0.9 * Runtime.getRuntime().maxMemory(); // 90% of maximum memory
                long availableMemory = ManagementFactory.getMemoryMXBean().getHeapMemoryUsage().getUsed();
                int availableProcessors = ManagementFactory.getOperatingSystemMXBean().getAvailableProcessors();

                if (availableMemory > maxMemory || availableProcessors < 2) {
                    Thread.sleep(Duration.ofMinutes(1).toMillis());
                }

                Instant startTime = Instant.now();
                ProcessBuilder builder = new ProcessBuilder()
                        .command(cmdArray)
                        .redirectErrorStream(true);

                try {
                    File file = Paths.get("./fileToDelete.txt").toFile();
                    if (file.exists()) Files.delete(Paths.get("./fileToDelete.txt"));

                    Process process = builder.start();
                    try (BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(process.getInputStream()))) {
                        String line;
                        while ((line = reader.readLine()) != null) {
                            System.out.println(line);
                        }
                    }

                    if (!process.waitFor(MAX_EXECUTION_TIME, TimeUnit.MILLISECONDS)) {
                        process.destroy();
                        throw new InterruptedException("Command execution time exceeded limit!");
                    }

                    Instant endTime = Instant.now();
                    return new ProcessResult(startTime, endTime, command, process.exitValue());
                } catch (InterruptedException | IOException e) {
                    throw new RuntimeException("Command execution failed", e);
                }
            });

            // Log the result of the command
            try {
                ProcessResult pr = result.get();
                String logMessage = String.format(
                        "{\"command\":\"%s\", \"startTime\":\"%s\", \"endTime\":\"%s\", \"exitValue\":%d}", 
                        pr.getCommand(), pr.getStartTime(), pr.getEndTime(), pr.getExitCode());
                new LoggerService().sendLog(logMessage);
            } catch (ExecutionException e) {
                System.err.println("Error executing command: " + command + ". Error message: " + e.getMessage());
            }
        }
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException, InterruptedException, ExecutionException {
        String[] commands = new String[]{"ls", "pwd"};
        new CommandExecutor().executeCommands(commands);
    }
}
``` 
The ProcessResult class is assumed to be defined as:

```java
import java.time.*;
public class ProcessResult {
    private Instant startTime;
    private Instant endTime;
    private String command;
    private int exitCode;

    public ProcessResult(Instant startTime, Instant endTime, String command, int exitCode) {
        this.startTime = startTime;
        this.endTime = endTime;
        this.command = command;
        this.exitCode = exitCode;
    }

    // Getters
}
```
Remember to replace LoggerService and EnvironmentConfigurator with actual implementation based on your requirements or libraries you're using. 

Please note that you need to manually call `System.gc()` after setting the process builder to make sure the memory usage reflects correctly. Additionally, be aware that calling `waitFor(MAX_EXECUTION_TIME, TimeUnit.MILLISECONDS)` will not stop the command itself if it's an infinite loop or similar, so you might need a different method of enforcing this limit depending on your needs.
']

