        while ((nread = fis.read(dataBytes)) != -1) {
            md.update(dataBytes, 0, nread);
        }

        byte[] mdbytes = md.digest();

        // Convert the byte to hex format
        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder("");
        for (int i = 0; i < mdbytes.length; i++) {
            sb.append(Integer.toString((mdbytes[i] & 0xff) + 0x100, 16).substring(1));
        }

        fis.close();
        return sb.toString();
    }
}
```
This method reads the file in chunks (with a buffer size of 8kb) to minimize memory usage, and updates the MD5 hash as it goes along. It also handles potential I/O bottlenecks by reading data sequentially from the file without seeking or skipping bytes, which could be slower.

