        report.append("Pokemon: ").append(pokemon.getName()).append("\n")
              .append("Type: ").append(type).append("\n")
              .append("Weaknesses: ").append(Arrays.toString(weaknesses)).append("\n")
              .append("Resistances: ").append(Arrays.toString(resistances)).append("\n");

        // Add any additional notes based on the weather conditions
        if (weather != null) {
            report.append("Weather Conditions: ").append(weather.getJSONArray("weather").getJSONObject(0).getString("main")).append("\n");
        } else {
            report.append("Unable to retrieve weather conditions\n");
        }

        // Save the Pokemon's performance data in the database
        db.saveReport(pokemon, report.toString());

        return report.toString();
    }

    private JSONObject getWeatherConditions(String location) {
        if (cachedWeatherResults.containsKey(location)) {
            // Return cached result if available
            return cachedWeatherResults.get(location);
        } else {
            try (CloseableHttpClient httpClient = HttpClients.createDefault()) {
                // Make a GET request to the weather API
                HttpGet request = new HttpGet(WEATHER_API + location);
                HttpResponse response = httpClient.execute(request);

                if (response.getStatusLine().getStatusCode() == 200) {
                    // Parse and cache the response
                    BufferedReader rd = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(response.getEntity().getContent()));
                    StringBuilder result = new StringBuilder();
                    String line;
                    while ((line = rd.readLine()) != null) {
                        result.append(line);
                    }

                    JSONObject weatherResult = new JSONObject(result.toString());
                    cachedWeatherResults.put(location, weatherResult);
                    return weatherResult;
                } else {
                    // Log and handle the error
                    System.err.println("Failed to retrieve weather conditions: " + response.getStatusLine().getReasonPhrase());
                }
            } catch (IOException e) {
                // Handle network errors gracefully
                System.err.println("Network error: " + e);
            }

            return null;
        }
    }
}
```
The above code is a simplified version of the solution, real implementation will need to consider many other factors and mechanisms like rate limiting, retry strategies, logging and monitoring etc. It also assumes that you have a database abstraction layer `PokemonDB` which can handle concurrent requests efficiently. This code does not include error handling for failed API calls or exceptions during JSON parsing.
