The second method initializes an AES-256 cipher using OpenSSL with a given password. It uses SHA-1 to derive a 32 bytes key from the password. The IV length is fixed at 16 bytes, as recommended by the AES-CBC mode of operation. After enabling the cipher in encryption mode, it logs out the context of the cipher for debugging or future reference.
