['Here is an example of how you might implement this method in Java:

```java
import java.io.*;
import java.lang.ref.SoftReference;
import java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicLong;
import java.util.logging.Level;
import java.util.logging.Logger;

public class StateLoader {
    private static final Logger logger = Logger.getLogger(StateLoader.class.getName());

    // Use a thread-safe atomic long to avoid synchronization issues
    private final AtomicLong lastModifiedTimestamp = new AtomicLong();
    private SoftReference<MoSTState> cachedObject = new SoftReference<>(null);

    public MoSTState loadStateFromFile(String filePath) {
        // Get the timestamp of the last modification attempt
        long currentLastModifiedTimestamp;
        try {
            currentLastModifiedTimestamp = getLastModificationTimeStamp(filePath);
        } catch (IOException e) {
            logger.log(Level.SEVERE, "Failed to get the file's timestamp", e);
            return null;
        }

        // Compare timestamps and check if the file was modified since last successful load
        long expectedLastModifiedTimestamp = lastModifiedTimestamp.get();
        MoSTState cachedObjectValue = cachedObject.get();
        if (currentLastModifiedTimestamp <= expectedLastModifiedTimestamp && cachedObjectValue != null) {
            return cachedObjectValue;
        } else {
            // Load the object from the file
            try (FileInputStream fis = new FileInputStream(filePath); 
                 ObjectInputStream ois = new ObjectInputStream(fis)) {
                MoSTState loadedObject = (MoSTState) ois.readObject();
                lastModifiedTimestamp.set(currentLastModifiedTimestamp);
                cachedObject = new SoftReference<>(loadedObject);
                logger.log(Level.INFO, "Successfully loaded the state object from file");
                return loadedObject;
            } catch (IOException | ClassNotFoundException e) {
                logger.log(Level.SEVERE, "Failed to load the state object from file", e);
                return null;
            }
        }
    }

    private long getLastModificationTimeStamp(String filePath) throws IOException {
        File file = new File(filePath);
        if (!file.exists()) {
            throw new FileNotFoundException("File not found: " + filePath);
        }
        return file.lastModified();
    }
}
```

Please note that this code assumes the `MoSTState` class to be serializable and the file path to be a local one, as handling network mounted storage systems would require additional logic, such as checking if the file is accessible before attempting to load it. Also, the thread-safety aspect was handled by using atomic variables and soft references to allow for concurrent access and garbage collection of the cached object when memory pressure is high.
']

