    private static final Logger logger = Logger.getLogger(ByteArrayDeserializer.class.getName());

    public <T> T deserialize(byte[] bytes, Class<T> clazz) {
        if (bytes == null || bytes.length < 4) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Invalid byte array");
        }

        int length = ((bytes[0] & 0xFF) << 24) | ((bytes[1] & 0xFF) << 16) | ((bytes[2] & 0xFF) << 8) | (bytes[3] & 0xFF);

        if (length != bytes.length - 4) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Byte array length does not match the declared length");
        }

        try (ByteArrayInputStream bais = new ByteArrayInputStream(Arrays.copyOfRange(bytes, 4, bytes.length));
             ObjectInputStream ois = new CheckedObjectInputStream(bais)) {
            ois.setBitsAllowed(true);
            ois.enableResolveMethod();
            return clazz.cast(ois.readObject());
        } catch (IOException e) {
            throw new RuntimeException("Failed to deserialize object", e);
        } catch (ClassNotFoundException e) {
            logger.warning("Missing class " + clazz.getName() + " during deserialization");
            return null;
        } catch (IllegalAccessException | InstantiationException e) {
            throw new RuntimeException("Failed to instantiate object", e);
        }
    }

    private static class CheckedObjectInputStream extends ObjectInputStream {
        public CheckedObjectInputStream(InputStream in) throws IOException {
            super(in);
        }

        @Override
        protected void finalize() throws Throwable {
            if (totBytes > MAX_MEMORY) {
                throw new OutOfMemoryError("Exceeded maximum memory limit of " + MAX_MEMORY + " bytes");
            }
            super.finalize();
        }
    }
}
```
This code defines a `ByteArrayDeserializer` class which has one method: `deserialize`. It first validates the byte array to ensure it starts with four bytes representing the length of the serialized data. Then, it deserializes the object and checks if the class is found or not. If an exception occurs during deserialization due to a corrupted byte array or invalid class, it throws a RuntimeException. Finally, it implements a mechanism to limit the amount of memory used during deserialization by overriding finalize method in custom ObjectInputStream subclass `CheckedObjectInputStream`.
']

