['Implementing such a complex system from scratch would be quite an undertaking, even for experienced Java developers. The code is too large to fit into one response so I'll provide a simplified version of what your function might look like and you can fill in the details as per your needs.

```java
public class MediaProcessor {
    private static final int MAX_CONCURRENT_OPS = 500;
    private static final String TRANSCODING_SERVICE_URL = "http://transcoding-service.com/";

    // Assume we have some API for transcoding service
    private TranscodingServiceAPI transcodingService;

    public MediaProcessor() {
        transcodingService = new TranscodingServiceAPI(TRANSCODING_SERVICE_URL);
    }

    public void streamAndProcessMediaFiles(List<File> files, List<TranscodeSetting> transcodeSettings) {
        ExecutorService executor = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(MAX_CONCURRENT_OPS);

        // Submit tasks to the executor
        for (int i = 0; i < files.size(); i++) {
            File file = files.get(i);
            TranscodeSetting setting = transcodeSettings.get(i % transcodeSettings.size());

            executor.submit(() -> processFile(file, setting));
        }

        // Wait for all tasks to complete
        executor.shutdown();
        try {
            if (!executor.awaitTermination(Long.MAX_VALUE, TimeUnit.NANOSECONDS)) {
                List<Runnable> abandonedTasks = executor.shutdownNow();
                System.out.println("Executor was abruptly shut down. The following tasks did not complete: " + abandonedTasks);
            }
        } catch (InterruptedException e) {
